<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zerafshan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zerafshan is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> that flows west from the mountains of Tajikistan through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, watering the oases of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>. Its valley was one of the richest agricultural and commercial regions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a> profile names the commercial centres along the Zerafshan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a> among the most productive urban centres of the khanate's heartland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zerafshan.jpg" alt="Zerafshan" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petar Milošević · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A0%D0%B5%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%97%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D1%88%D0%B0%D0%BD_%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%BB%D0%B5_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%9F%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B4%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%82_(river_Zarafshon_by_Panjakent).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
